<Base title="Terms of use · Shift" description="The terms for using Shift, an email app for macOS made by TALKK." path="/terms">
  <main id="main" class="wrap doc">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 25 November 2026</p>

    <p>These terms cover your use of Shift, an email app for macOS made by TALKK ("we") in Byron Bay, Australia. By installing or using Shift you agree to them.</p>

    <h2>Using Shift</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Shift is a client for your own email accounts. Your email provider's terms continue to apply to your use of its service, including Google's for Gmail.</li>
      <li>You're responsible for the email you send with Shift and for keeping your Mac secure.</li>
      <li>Don't use Shift to send spam, break the law, or interfere with your email provider's services.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your data</h2>
    <p>Your mail and account stay yours. How Shift handles them is set out in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, which forms part of these terms.</p>

    <h2>Permanent actions</h2>
    <p>Some actions can't be undone, such as Empty Trash, Empty Spam and deleting a label. Shift asks for confirmation first, and the result is the same as doing it in your email provider's own app.</p>

    <h2>Early versions</h2>
    <p>Shift is under active development. Features may change, and early versions may contain bugs. Keep in mind that your mail always remains with your email provider, so Shift can be removed at any time without losing it.</p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
